  "term": "XYY syndrome",
  "definition": "XYY syndrome is a genetic condition in a male with an extra Y chromosome, producing a 47,XYY chromosome pattern. It is often linked with tall stature, a higher chance of learning disabilities, and delays in speech and language development.",
